\title{epidemicdates: impute missing symptom onsets in line lists}
\description{
Some line lists fill a missing onset date with the report date minus a
delay drawn from the pooled empirical onset-to-report delays of cases with
both dates.
This is back-sampling.
\code{epidemicdates} applies back-sampling and three alternatives to a real
line list.
It is the R version of the core line-list tools in the Python package
\code{epidemic_dates} and the JavaScript module \code{epidemic-dates.js}.
}
